%I A402106 #4 Nov 18 2026 20:08:25
%S A402106 0,0,0,0,1,0,1,1,0,1,2,1,2,1,1,0,3,1,3,0,1,2,3,0,0,2,2,0,4,0,4,0,2,3,
%T A402106 0,0,5,3,2,0,5,0,5,1,1,3,5,0,0,1,3,1,6,1,1,0,3,4,6,1,6,4,1,0,1,1,7,2,
%U A402106 3,1,7,1,7,5,1,2,1,1,7,1
%N A402106 Difference between the integer parts of the square roots of the upper and lower central divisors of n.
%C A402106 Called the shell discrepancy of n in Baloui (2026), where d_1(n) = max{d | n : d <= sqrt(n)} = A033676(n) is the lower central divisor and d_2(n) = n/d_1(n) = A033677(n) is the upper central divisor of n.
%C A402106 This sequence is the case r = 2 of the r-degree shell discrepancy family c^(r)(n) = floor(A033677(n)^(1/r)) - floor(A033676(n)^(1/r)) (r >= 1), which measures the distance between d_1(n) and d_2(n) across r-th power shells [k^r, (k + 1)^r - 1]. The linear case r = 1 recovers c^(1)(n) = A033677(n) - A033676(n) = A056737(n), related to the factor-difference sets studied by Erdos and Rosenfeld (1997). The general family c^(r)(n), its minimal multipliers beta_m^(r)(n) = min{k >= 1 : c^(r)(k*n) = m}, and their connection to the Riemann zeta values zeta(r + 1) are studied in Baloui (2026).
%C A402106 In the quadratic case r = 2, integers n with a(n) = 0 are called balanced (counted in [k^2, k^2 + 2*k] by A382306), and integers with a(n) >= 1 are called eccentric (with solutions to a(n) = 1 in [k^2, k^2 + 2*k] counted by A383115).
%C A402106 A382286(n) is the least k >= 1 such that a(k*n) = 0, and A381054(n) is the least k >= 1 such that a(k*n) = 1.
%C A402106 For k >= 3 and n in [k^2, k^2 + 2*k], a(n) = k - 1 if and only if n is prime, whereas every composite n in [k^2, k^2 + 2*k] (k >= 2) satisfies a(n) <= floor((k + 1)/sqrt(2)) - 1. Consequently, for every k >= 6, no integer in [k^2, k^2 + 2*k] attains a value m in the interval floor((k + 1)/sqrt(2)) - 1 < m < k - 1.
%C A402106 Cumulative counts satisfy #{n <= x : a(n) = 0} = (2/3)*x^(3/4) + O(x^(1/2)) and, for each fixed m >= 1, #{n <= x : a(n) = m} = (4/3)*x^(3/4) + O_m(x^(1/2)).
%D A402106 P. Erdos and M. Rosenfeld, The factor-difference set of integers, Acta Arith. 79 (1997), 353-359.
%H A402106 Hassan Baloui, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24109171">The Minimal Balancing Multiplier and the Riemann Zeta Function at Positive Integers</a>, Zenodo preprint, 2026.
%F A402106 a(n) = floor(sqrt(A033677(n))) - floor(sqrt(A033676(n))) = A000196(A033677(n)) - A000196(A033676(n)).
%F A402106 a(n^2) = 0 and a(n*(n + 1)) = 0 for all n >= 1.
%F A402106 a(p) = A000196(p) - 1 for all primes p.
%F A402106 a(n) = 0 if and only if A382286(n) = 1.
%F A402106 a(n) = 1 if and only if A381054(n) = 1.
%F A402106 a(n) <= floor((A000196(n) + 1)/sqrt(2)) - 1 for all composite n >= 4.
%e A402106 For n = 6, the central divisors are d_1(6) = 2 and d_2(6) = 3, so a(6) = floor(sqrt(3)) - floor(sqrt(2)) = 1 - 1 = 0.
%e A402106 For n = 12, the central divisors are d_1(12) = 3 and d_2(12) = 4, so a(12) = floor(sqrt(4)) - floor(sqrt(3)) = 2 - 1 = 1.
%e A402106 For n = 17 (prime), d_1(17) = 1 and d_2(17) = 17, so a(17) = floor(sqrt(17)) - 1 = 4 - 1 = 3.
%e A402106 For n = 22, the central divisors are d_1(22) = 2 and d_2(22) = 11, so a(22) = floor(sqrt(11)) - floor(sqrt(2)) = 3 - 1 = 2.
%o A402106 (PARI) a(n) = my(d=divisors(n), c=d[(#d+1)\2]); sqrtint(n\c) - sqrtint(c);
%Y A402106 Cf. A000040, A000196, A000290, A002378, A033676, A033677, A056737, A381054, A382286, A382306, A383115, A401528.
%K A402106 nonn,easy,new
%O A402106 1,11
%A A402106 _Hassan Baloui_, Nov 13 2026
